From dd641bba19a606473e3fbb435bb46692d27b1d25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:29:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat(client): expose the card-text language setting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the settings control for the `cardTextLanguage` preference next to the
card-art one, with the same `SegmentedControl` shape and the same endonym labels
(the two vocabularies coincide today — both exclude `pl` — but stay separate, so
the label table is bound to `CardTextLanguage` rather than reusing the art map).

Translations are real rather than the usual "copy the English string and let the
fallback handle it": the two controls sit adjacent and read almost identically in
English ("Card art language" / "Card text language"), so a copied string would
have labelled the text setting as the art one in seven languages. Added for
en/es/fr/de/it/pt/pl/ja.
